A classic example at the beginning of learning programming.
`hello.c` is the source file.

@[hello.c@=
@<hello@:executable@:Language@/C@/Module@/module@>
@

@<hello@:executable@:Language@/C@/Module@/main body@=
printf("Hello World!\n");
@~ Project@/hello@/topics@/output @
The command has a single usage without options or arguments.
@<hello@:executable@:UI@/Command Line@/invocation syntax@=
{
    name: 'hello',
}
@